+#
+# KCrash's implementation is sigaction()/sigemptyset()/SA_RESTART signal
+# handlers that, on a crash, fork() a child, setgid()/setuid() it, exec()
+# drkonqi, waitpid() for it and alarm() a watchdog. Every one of those symbols
+# is absent from wasi-libc, because wasip2 has no asynchronous signals and no
+# fork/exec at all -- 15 distinct undefined identifiers in kcrash.cpp alone,
+# plus <QUnhandledException> in exception.cpp (FEATURE_thread=OFF). This is not
+# a header guard away; it is the one framework in KCalc's graph with no
+# meaningful wasm implementation.
+#
+# Building a KCrash that COMPILED would mean gutting kcrash.cpp until
+# KCrash::initialize() did nothing -- a stub pretending to be a framework,
+# which is worse than an honest absence. So KCalc runs with no crash handler
+# on this platform. When a wk node traps, wasmtime reports it to the host and
+# the node dies; that is wk's crash story, not drkonqi's.
